{"task_id":"sample_93018156077f8355","acceptance_criteria":["Calling xmltodict.parse with disable_entities=True on an internal XML bomb DOCTYPE raises expat.ExpatError instead of returning a parsed dictionary or None.","The expat.ExpatError raised for disabled entity handling includes the substring 'entities are disabled'.","Calling xmltodict.parse with disable_entities=True on an XML document declaring an external entity/DTD raises expat.ExpatError instead of producing {'root': None} or attempting entity resolution.","Calling xmltodict.parse on ordinary XML containing a comment, such as '<a><!-- ignored --><b>1</b></a>', still returns {'a': {'b': '1'}}.","Calling xmltodict.parse with disable_entities=False preserves the existing entity-expansion behavior for the XML bomb document."],"user_fact_sheet":[{"topic":"Security expectation","fact":"If entities are disabled, entity-related constructs should cause an immediate failure rather than being silently dropped or represented as None."},{"topic":"Error type","fact":"The user expects the failure to be an expat.ExpatError, not a generic ValueError or custom exception."},{"topic":"Error message","fact":"The error message should make clear that entities are disabled; the exact full message is not more important than including that idea."},{"topic":"Comments","fact":"Ordinary XML comments should remain allowed and ignored normally, even when entity handling is disabled."},{"topic":"Backward compatibility","fact":"When disable_entities=False, existing behavior should not be broken."}],"fail_to_pass":["test::tests.test_xmltodict::test_disable_entities_true_rejects_xmlbomb","test::tests.test_xmltodict::test_disable_entities_true_rejects_external_dtd"],"pass_to_pass":["tests.test_dicttoxml::test_root","tests.test_dicttoxml::test_simple_cdata","tests.test_dicttoxml::test_cdata","tests.test_dicttoxml::test_attrib","tests.test_dicttoxml::test_attrib_and_cdata","tests.test_dicttoxml::test_list","tests.test_dicttoxml::test_list_ex